                <pb facs="0190" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg82"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 14.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson announces that the naval officers of Great Britain have ceased
                    protecting their shipping upon a notice given by Da Gama to the foreign
                    commanders that he is about to make an effort to stop merchandise from being
                    landed.</p>
            </div>
